Performance Enhancements (DRYAD):
- Must abide simulation distance:
  - Any animations. From textures to entities.
  - Rendering instances. We must check whether skipping rendering based on distance would be worthwhile
    - If yes, then fade them in/out rather than allowing pop-in
  - Particle logic.
  - Advanced physics application.
  - Runtime instance spawning. Any instance that's being spawned too far, gets enqueued until the player gets close enough.
Per-entity render flags, set during the SimDistance check collision already runs:
- render.animatedTexture: texture gate ORs its owners' flags instead of testing every owner AABB per frame.
- render.model: skip rendering distant entities entirely. Reaches into the decal and translucent passes, so it's its own pass.
- Force the SimDistance check even when an entity's collision flag is off.
- Entity-owned textures only. Large static owners (sea-surface, terrain, obstacles) keep point-to-AABB.
- Multi-owner still needs the OR. energy-core resolves two owners at different distances.


Additions to Level API:
- Entities:
  - GetState(entityId)
  - GetAll
  - Animate(entityId, ...)
  - Kill(entityId)
  - Delete(entityId)
  - Heal(entityId, amount)
  - SetPhysics(entityId, ...)
  - SetMeta(entityId, ...)
  - SetPosition(entityId)
  - SetScale(entityId)
  - Damage(objectType, id, amount)
  - SetAction(entityId, ...)
  - SetNpcBehavior(entityId, ...)
  - NpcAccessories
- Player:
  - Animate
  - CharacterSwitch
  - SetPosition
  - SetScale
  - SetMeta
  - SetAction
  - Kill
  - Heal
  - Damage
  - Launch(velocity) — sets velocity and the `launched` flag together, so games can make the player lose their footing.
  - Accessories
  - GetState
- Spawn:
  - Terrain
  - Obstacle
  - Entity
  - Trigger
- Camera:
  - Switch
  - SetPosition
  - GetPosition
  - GetDirection — aim-where-you-look needs camera forward; today it's GetActiveLevel().cameraConfig.state.forward.
  - Snapshot
- Trigger(triggerId)
- Do:
  -
- GetSnapshot
- Per-frame hook (callback or LEVEL_TICK), so games stop running their own rAF loop one frame out of phase with the sim.
- IsPaused()
- LEVEL_PAUSED carries its source (player vs PauseLevel()), so a game-over freeze doesn't need a game-side flag.


Add full documentation API so devs can understand how to work the engine.


Create a level interpreter that reads level json data and returns 2D representations of the level.
- The output can be ASCII/data (for AI)
- The output can be JPEGs
- Output can be multiple. Things stacked on top of each other are hard to define, so each piece of output should reflect a height region based on the height differences in objects (aka dynamic)


Allow special rotational control so Carl can rotate in water with Q and E
- Line up to things you want to attach to.
- A and D controls change direction.


Version Goals:
- 0.32: Main Update Released [FINISHED]
- 0.33: Decal Rework [FINISHED]
  1. Pre-load Simulator Cache with player-characters and all templates. [DONE]
  2. Jump Window Expansion (ground probe so early presses can register early; tiny window after losing ground contact) [DONE]
    - Make rendering obey FrameRate. [DONE]
  3. Sticky Terrain: [DONE]
    - Fix bug where you clip out of bounds in voids. [DONE]
    - Add a "sticky" field to terrain. The player's grounding is no longer tied to a minimum speed while grounded on this part. [DONE]
- 0.34: Camera & Controls Stability [PATCHING]
    - Offset the camera at incline changes so it remains vertically stationary during loops. Ensure it doesn't influence movement. [DONE]
  1. Loop detection false positives [DONE]
    - The upward slope in the tunnel connecting underwater and above water counts as a loop, forcing a bad side-view camera angle.
  2. Backface Culling [DONE]
    - Fix Water vs Trigger layering. [DONE]
  3.  Toon-switch for outlines. [DONE]
  4. DEFERRED Performance Enhancements [CURRENT]
    - Move Render.js Shaders to new Shaders.js module. [DONE]
    - Move Object.js shape functions to new NewPrimitive.js module. [DONE]
      - Center the pyramid: its base sits at y=0, so the bottom-center lift floats it by half its height. Carl has pyramid-hosted decals, so check him after. [DONE]
  5. Interpolation [PENDING]
  6. Todo Performance Enhancements [PENDING]
  7. Occlusion Culling [PENDING]
    - Measure first: a one-off debug count (GPU occlusion queries) of how much drawing is fully hidden behind walls. Build only if it beats the CPU cost.
    - If built: same-frame CPU depth check in new math/Occlusion.js. Scope: docs/scoping/render/culling-scope.md §4.5.
  8. orbitCam Rework [PENDING]
    - Games can't set the initial camera yaw or the player's spawn facing (LSM rotated its whole level 180° to work around it).
    - Mouse sensitivity is read once at level start, so a settings change mid-level does nothing until the next level.
  9. Sprite/Bilboard Support (rotating images that resize based on distance)
  10. Movement Enhancements. [PENDING]
    - Release jump early for quicker falloff.
    - Solve over-rotation in above-water tunnel.
    - Store medium (Water/Air) on entity definition (e.g. playerState)
    - If holding "A", then pressing and releasing "D", "A" stops working until it's pressed again. This must be fixed.
- 0.35: Workers (Multi-Threading) [PENDING]
  - Needs a full scoping pass.
  - Consider a coordinator/state manager. If small, an exported "Workforce" object in meta.js acting as the state manager could work quite well.
  - Main candidate for worker deferral: noise textures (lvl2 water face bake is ~1.3 s of a ~3.4 s load).
  - Entity AI (0.36) may benefit: pathfinding is expensive both while building and in the hot path.
  - Afterwards: look for hot-path candidates (e.g. animated noise re-bakes).
- 0.36: Entity AI
  - Blueprint movement fields chase, jump, jumpOnSight, disappear and aggroRange validate but do nothing; devs read them as the AI API.
  1. Add optional Q/W rotation controls & add full custom player controls support.
  2. Add optional Swimming & Flying states.
  3. Add player/characters.json animation authoring support.
  x. Bug fixes.
- 0.37: Additional Control Schemes
  - Controller Support.
  - Custom control bindings.
    - Add gameplay controls bindings to API_CONFIG so games don't have to run custom event listeners (they still can if they want).
      - Standard movement and camera controls have defaults.
      - Any abilities for the player authored in the level payload are added as extra properties for authoring in the config (needs a function that also emits logs for added and removed API fields).
      - Any of these can be changed to "none" and the engine stops listening for those.
      - A full 
      - The Simulator has a hardcoded controls scheme.
  - Input magnitude is ignored: Movement normalizes the direction, so forward: 0.5 is full speed. Analog sticks need it.
  - No invert-Y option.
- 0.38: Combat Expansion
  - Player hp is a stale 3 nothing reads; damage is ring rules only. Games build hearts/HP/i-frames themselves.
  - One enemy hit soft-locks the player: Stunned and invulnerable are set, but nothing counts the timer down or leaves Stunned before respawn.
  x. Bug fixes.
