- 1.0: Full API & Documentation
  - Add canonSchemas aliases.
  - Improve validation errors and warnings.
    - Errors only give the generic path, not the actual degenerate entry.
    - Errors don't disclose how many sibling or child entries are affected/lost.
  - Improve engine processes logging.
  - Remove Unit and UnitVector3 from the Engine API. Games read and write raw vectors; the API restores instancing on write and strips it on read.
    - Complaint: one object mixes types (transform.position/velocity are UnitVector3, scale and facing are plain), and .set(x, y, z) silently writes undefined.
  - Game-developer API reference: StartupGuide stops at the title screen and system_map is engine-internal. LSM found the API by dumping ENGINE in the console.
- 1.1: CarlNet Editor
  - Transform the Simulator App to a proper 3D editor.
    - It will be capable of adding, resizing and moving objects to build models.
    - This allows the building of entities, bosses, obstacles and terrain chunks.
  - Controls ideas:
    - Click to select an object, an action wheel opens that lets you select what control scheme to use (positioning, scaling, etc)
      - That same scheme opens for that object in the UI for data-driven editing, including access to the json.
      - The different views are synced and highlight when updating together.
    - Right-click to deselect the current object(s) so you can select a new one (or multiple)
    - Drag to select multiple objects, the same action wheel opens, but greys out single-target options.
